  "chapter": {
    "number": 121,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(122) A Song of Degrees."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I was glad when they said to me, Let us go into the house of the Lord.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Our feet stood in your courts, O Jerusalem.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Jerusalem is built as a city whose fellowship is complete.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For there the tribes went up, the tribes of the Lord, as a testimony for Israel, to give thanks to the name of the Lord.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For there are set thrones for judgment, even thrones for the house of David.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "noteId": 229
          },
          {
            "text": "Pray now for the peace of Jerusalem: and let there be prosperity to them that love you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let peace, I pray, be within your host, and prosperity in your palaces.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For the sake of my brethren and my neighbors, I have indeed spoken peace concerning you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Because of the house of the Lord our God, I have diligently sought your good.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 229,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Or, ask Jerusalem how it is with her.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 121,
          "verse": 6
        }
      }
    ]
  },
